   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing and directing the department of health to do research and study as to the effects of psychostimulants, selective seratonin reuptake inhibitors, antidepressants and other drugs which are prescribed for attention deficit disorders, ADD and ADHD, for school age children",
    "basePrintNo": "S8202",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8202-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Health, Commissioner of",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8202\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act\nauthorizing and directing the department of health to\ndo research and study\nas to the effects of psychostimulants, selective seratonin reuptake\ninhibitors, antidepressants and other drugs which are prescribed for\nattention deficit disorders, ADD and ADHD, for school age children\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF THE BILL:\n\nTo conduct a study on drugs prescribed for school-age children with\nADD and ADHD, making recommendations thereafter.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nAuthorizes the commissioner of health, in conjunction with the\ncommissioner of mental health, the commissioner of mental retardation\nand developmental disabilities, and the commissioner of education to\nconduct a study and do research as to the effect of psycho\nstimulants, selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors, antidepressants\nand other drugs prescribed for ADD and ADHD, in school age children.\nThe commissioner shall report his or her findings to the governor,\nthe speaker of the assembly and the temporary president of the senate\nwithin two years that this act shall take effect.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently 5 million school kids in America are on psychotropic drugs\nthat are prescribed and administered by their schools. (Insight\nMagazine, June 1996). Kids are routinely being misdiagnosed and\nforced to take drugs for behavior problems, often containing violent\nside effects. This problem is becoming an epidemic with no end in\nsight. It is an imperative that the commissioner of health performs a\nstudy on the effect of medicating our school children, and making\nrecommendations thereafter.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2009: A.5602 - Passed Assembly\n2008: A.5388 - Passed Assembly\n2007: A.5388 - Passed Assembly\n2006: A.5885A - Passed Assembly\n2005: A.5885 - Health\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to state government.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
